021/250000000000` |\n| 993 | 31.983895593654374 | `15992420545053/500000000000` |\n| 994 | 31.992883399257602 | `15996822807313/500000000000` |\n| 995 | 31.994174058188146 | `3199478454971/100000000000` |\n| 996 | 31.994174058188146 | `3199478454971/100000000000` |\n| 997 | 31.996875920326034 | `15999150334837/500000000000` |\n| 998 | 31.996875920294037 | `31998301106111/1000000000000` |\n\n**Certificate.** Exact rational `n S` / `x y t` witnesses in `certificates/`, with the archive's SHA-256 checksum above. The ZIP will be attached directly to this public issue, rather than to a submitter-owned GitHub repository.\n\n**Checking.** Two separately implemented exact checkers (SAT and polygon intersection),\nthe maintainer's unmodified text checker, original text and SVG-round-trip interval checks.\nThe attached archive includes a standalone exact-rational SAT feasibility checker:\n`python3 verify_public.py certificates/n328.cert` (substitute the other certificate filenames as needed).\nThe interval and geometry-check receipts are retained in the included JSON files.\nPer-case counts/timings and arithmetic are in proof receipts. Original exact/text CPU\ntimings include those stages; later subprocess costs are not a total charged CPU tally.\nChecks ran in finite eight-CPU Flair Docker containers as UID3556:GID100; no search ran.\n\n**What the checkers share.** Both exact checkers come from the same upstream repository\nand share input certificates, rational half-angle representation, Python Fraction and\ncircumscribed-disc broad phase. The interval route shares SAT geometry.\n\n[01-squares-100-certificates-and-poses.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33685905/01-squares-100-certificates-and-poses.zip)\n\n**Not done.** Worldwide report-order priority reconciliation, unrestricted local/global\noptimality, rigidity and exhaustive comparison to every theoretical construction remain\nunproved. Catalogue/registry inclusion is requested, not assumed. Scope is in EVIDENCE.md.\n\n**Lineage and credit.** Complete upstream square solver plus public/neighboring seeds and\ngrow–crop–optimize continuation. Some rows are deletions, borders or subset crops; keep\ntheir parent/source attribution. Per-case provenance is retained. Not 100 independent\nnew arrangements. Cross-posted copies of the same release should retain one provenance.\n\n**AI assistance.** OpenAI Codex assisted the checking and packaging.\n\n— Darius Muglich\n\n[01-squares-100-certificates-and-poses.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33685972/01-squares-100-certificates-and-poses.zip)\n"
